<p>The first line calls for 4 1/2 cups of flour, because 1 Kings 4:22 reads &#8220;And Solomon&#8217;s provision for one day was thirty measures of fine flour, and threescore measures of meal.&#8221; In the same way, the rest refer respectively to butter, sugar, raisins, figs, almonds, milk, honey, salt, leaven, and eggs. No baking instructions are given.</p>
